{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014oiCHbV1f3nZ4nxVBmyw2e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"ner_llama_conll\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003, N=8 inference. Cross-model validation for model-agnostic QE claims.\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"greedy_f1\": 0.921,\n7\t      \"oracle_f1\": 0.944,\n8\t      \"oracle_headroom_pp\": 2.3,\n9\t      \"SJ_rho_full\": 0.418,\n10\t      \"FK_rho_full\": 0.405,\n11\t      \"LP_rho_full\": 0.298,\n12\t      \"EM_rho_full\": 0.421,\n13\t      \"voting_conf_rho_full\": 0.413,\n14\t      \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.694,\n15\t      \"EM_AUROC\": 0.701,\n16\t      \"LP_AUROC\": 0.752,\n17\t      \"selection_SJ_f1\": 0.92,\n18\t      \"selection_LP_f1\": 0.921,\n19\t      \"selection_vs_greedy_pp\": -0.1,\n20\t      \"structural_beats_surface\": true,\n21\t      \"degeneracy_rate\": 0.55\n22\t    },\n23\t    \"tables\": [\n24\t      {\n25\t        \"name\": \"Table: LLaMA CoNLL-2003 QE Metrics (N=8, T=1.0)\",\n26\t        \"columns\": [\n27\t          \"Signal\",\n28\t          \"ρ_full\",\n29\t          \"τ_full\",\n30\t          \"AUROC\",\n31\t          \"ECE\",\n32\t          \"Sel_F1\"\n33\t        ],\n34\t        \"rows\": [\n35\t          [\n36\t            \"SJ\",\n37\t            0.418,\n38\t            0.372,\n39\t            0.694,\n40\t            0.112,\n41\t            0.92\n42\t          ],\n43\t          [\n44\t            \"FK\",\n45\t            0.405,\n46\t            0.361,\n47\t            0.688,\n48\t            0.108,\n49\t            0.919\n50\t          ],\n51\t          [\n52\t            \"EM\",\n53\t            0.421,\n54\t            0.377,\n55\t            0.701,\n56\t            0.105,\n57\t            0.919\n58\t          ],\n59\t          [\n60\t            \"Voting_conf\",\n61\t            0.413,\n62\t            0.368,\n63\t            0.698,\n64\t            0.092,\n65\t            0.92\n66\t          ],\n67\t          [\n68\t            \"Logprob\",\n69\t            0.298,\n70\t            0.238,\n71\t            0.752,\n72\t            0.131,\n73\t            0.921\n74\t          ],\n75\t          [\n76\t            \"Greedy\",\n77\t            \"—\",\n78\t            \"—\",\n79\t            \"—\",\n80\t            \"—\",\n81\t            0.921\n82\t          ],\n83\t          [\n84\t            \"Oracle\",\n85\t            \"—\",\n86\t            \"—\",\n87\t            \"—\",\n88\t            \"—\",\n89\t            0.944\n90\t          ]\n91\t        ]\n92\t      }\n93\t    ],\n94\t    \"figures\": [],\n95\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model validation holds but provides incremental rather than decisive evidence. Reviewer likely notes: (1) both are 8B-class models — no evidence for smaller/larger scales; (2) CoNLL's high baseline makes selection analysis trivial (headroom <3pp). In median tier, this supports the QE contribution as 'solid engineering' (A1 PARTIAL) but doesn't push novelty score above 3-4 because the finding (structural signals generalize across architectures) is expected from UQ literature.\\n\\n在 median 档下，LLaMA CoNLL 复现 Qwen CoNLL 的核心模式（structural > surface，selection ≈ greedy），但不会显著超越。CoNLL 高 baseline F1 (>0.91) 导致高 degeneracy (~55%)，oracle headroom 仅 2.3pp，selection 无法显著超过 greedy。SJ_rho ~0.42 与 Qwen CoNLL (0.436) 一致，验证 cross-model 但 reviewer 会指出 '两个 8B 模型不足以证明 model-agnostic'——这正是 A6 PARTIAL 假设的体现。LP AUROC 偏高（0.75）因为 CoNLL 高精度实例的 LP 能有效区分 perfect vs near-perfect，但 rho 仍低于 structural signals。\"\n96\t  },\n97\t  {\n98\t    \"name\": \"simple_verifier_baseline\",\n99\t    \"description\": \"Logistic regression on 5 QE signals as supervised verifier. Tests whether oracle gap is closable with supervision. Training on SciERC NER+RE with F1 labels.\",\n100\t    \"results\": {\n101\t      \"ner_verifier_selection_f1\": 0.655,\n102\t      \"ner_greedy_f1\": 0.644,\n103\t      \"ner_oracle_f1\": 0.776,\n104\t      \"ner_gap_closure_pct\": 8.3,\n105\t      \"ner_verifier_vs_greedy_pp\": 1.1,\n106\t      \"re_verifier_selection_f1\": 0.412,\n107\t      \"re_greedy_f1\": 0.404,\n108\t      \"re_oracle_f1\": 0.585,\n109\t      \"re_gap_closure_pct\": 4.4,\n110\t      \"re_verifier_vs_greedy_pp\": 0.8,\n111\t      \"cv_auroc_ner\": 0.772,\n112\t      \"cv_auroc_re\": 0.718,\n113\t      \"feature_importance_top\": \"EM > voting_conf > SJ > LP > FK\",\n114\t      \"overfitting_risk\": \"moderate (n=529 NER, n=397 RE, 5-fold CV)\",\n115\t      \"training_time_minutes\": 12\n116\t    },\n117\t    \"tables\": [\n118\t      {\n119\t        \"name\": \"Table: Supervised Verifier vs Unsupervised Signals (5-fold CV)\",\n120\t        \"columns\": [\n121\t          \"Method\",\n122\t          \"NER Sel_F1\",\n123\t          \"NER Δ_greedy\",\n124\t          \"NER Gap%\",\n125\t          \"RE Sel_F1\",\n126\t          \"RE Δ_greedy\",\n127\t          \"RE Gap%\"\n128\t        ],\n129\t        \"rows\": [\n130\t          [\n131\t            \"Greedy (T=0)\",\n132\t            0.644,\n133\t            \"—\",\n134\t            \"—\",\n135\t            0.404,\n136\t            \"—\",\n137\t            \"—\"\n138\t          ],\n139\t          [\n140\t            \"Best unsupervised (LP)\",\n141\t            0.65,\n142\t            \"+0.6pp\",\n143\t            \"4.5%\",\n144\t            0.409,\n145\t            \"+0.5pp\",\n146\t            \"2.8%\"\n147\t          ],\n148\t          [\n149\t            \"LR verifier (5 signals)\",\n150\t            0.655,\n151\t            \"+1.1pp\",\n152\t            \"8.3%\",\n153\t            0.412,\n154\t            \"+0.8pp\",\n155\t            \"4.4%\"\n156\t          ],\n157\t          [\n158\t            \"Oracle\",\n159\t            0.776,\n160\t            \"+13.2pp\",\n161\t            \"100%\",\n162\t            0.585,\n163\t            \"+18.1pp\",\n164\t            \"100%\"\n165\t          ]\n166\t        ]\n167\t      },\n168\t      {\n169\t        \"name\": \"Table: Feature Importance (Logistic Regression Coefficients, NER)\",\n170\t        \"columns\": [\n171\t          \"Signal\",\n172\t          \"Mean Coeff\",\n173\t          \"Std across folds\"\n174\t        ],\n175\t        \"rows\": [\n176\t          [\n177\t            \"EM\",\n178\t            0.42,\n179\t            0.08\n180\t          ],\n181\t          [\n182\t            \"voting_conf\",\n183\t            0.31,\n184\t            0.06\n185\t          ],\n186\t          [\n187\t            \"SJ\",\n188\t            0.22,\n189\t            0.09\n190\t          ],\n191\t          [\n192\t            \"logprob\",\n193\t            0.18,\n194\t            0.11\n195\t          ],\n196\t          [\n197\t            \"FK\",\n198\t            0.07,\n199\t            0.05\n200\t          ]\n201\t        ]\n202\t      }\n203\t    ],\n204\t    \"figures\": [],\n205\t    \"analysis\": \"Verifier closes 8.3% of NER gap — statistically significant (paired t-test p<0.05 across folds) but practically marginal. This is precisely the A5 WEAK outcome: enough to say 'supervision helps' but not enough to constitute a paper contribution. One reviewer will say 'you showed logistic regression on your own features slightly beats your own features used individually — this is expected and not interesting.' Counter-argument: the 92% gap that remains proves the signals are fundamentally limited, not just suboptimally combined. Paper frames as: 'preliminary supervised baseline confirms gap is partially closable, motivating dedicated learned verifiers as future work.' Findings-level contribution at best for this component.\\n\\n在 median 档下 (A5 FAILS/WEAK)，trained verifier 完成但 gap closure <15%。逻辑回归在 5 个高度相关的信号上（SJ-LP pearson=0.57）受限于 feature redundancy——exp-016 已经显示 ensemble 无优势。NER gap closure ~8% (1.1pp) 因为：(1) 监督信号确实比 unsupervised heuristic 好（能学到非线性组合），但 (2) 输入信号本身信息量有限（within-instance discriminative power 低），5-fold CV 在 n=529 上容易 overfit。RE 更弱 (4.4%) 因为 binary dominance (43% F1=0) 使得回归主要学到 'zero vs non-zero' 而非 quality gradient。Reviewer 评价：'path forward evidence suggestive not definitive'——8% closure 不足以作为独立贡献，但支持 'trained verifiers needed' 的 future work framing。\"\n206\t  },\n207\t  {\n208\t    \"name\": \"claim_audit\",\n209\t    \"description\": \"Systematic numerical consistency audit across all paper sections. Resolve contradictions between Discussion, Limitations, Abstract, and source experiment data.\",\n210\t    \"results\": {\n211\t      \"contradictions_found\": 4,\n212\t      \"critical_contradictions\": 1,\n213\t      \"minor_inconsistencies\": 3,\n214\t      \"sections_affected\": [\n215\t        \"Discussion\",\n216\t        \"Limitations\",\n217\t        \"Abstract\",\n218\t        \"Introduction\"\n219\t      ],\n220\t      \"resolution_time_hours\": 3,\n221\t      \"key_contradiction_1\": \"Discussion '+0.1pp over single-sample' vs Limitations '+0.4pp over greedy' — source truth is +0.6pp (logprob NER, exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap)\",\n222\t      \"key_contradiction_2\": \"Abstract AUROC '0.82' refers to CoNLL EM (0.816) but body text reports SciERC EM (0.749) — need to clarify which dataset/metric the abstract claim uses\",\n223\t      \"key_contradiction_3\": \"Introduction claims '5 confidence signals across 4 families' but method section describes 5 signals in 3 families (structural: SJ/FK/EM; voting: VC; probabilistic: LP)\",\n224\t      \"key_contradiction_4\": \"Capability-degeneracy numbers: Discussion says 'CoNLL 58%' but exp_012_rerun_1024 shows tied_fraction=0.597 for constrained, referencing different definitions of degeneracy\"\n225\t    },\n226\t    \"tables\": [\n227\t      {\n228\t        \"name\": \"Table: Claim Audit Results\",\n229\t        \"columns\": [\n230\t          \"Location\",\n231\t          \"Claimed Value\",\n232\t          \"Source Truth\",\n233\t          \"Resolution\"\n234\t        ],\n235\t        \"rows\": [\n236\t          [\n237\t            \"Abstract: 'AUROC up to 0.82'\",\n238\t            \"0.82\",\n239\t            \"CoNLL EM 0.816 (N=8) or 0.841 (N=16)\",\n240\t            \"Use 0.82 rounded from 0.816, cite N=8 CoNLL\"\n241\t          ],\n242\t          [\n243\t            \"Discussion: '+0.1pp'\",\n244\t            \"+0.1pp over single-sample\",\n245\t            \"+0.6pp LP vs greedy (NER, p=0.39 n.s.)\",\n246\t            \"Correct to '+0.6pp (n.s., p=0.39)'\"\n247\t          ],\n248\t          [\n249\t            \"Limitations: '+0.4pp'\",\n250\t            \"+0.4pp over greedy\",\n251\t            \"Same metric different rounding\",\n252\t            \"Unify to +0.6pp with CI\"\n253\t          ],\n254\t          [\n255\t            \"Intro: '4 families'\",\n256\t            \"4 signal families\",\n257\t            \"3 families (structural/voting/probabilistic)\",\n258\t            \"Correct to '3 families' or redefine EM as separate family\"\n259\t          ]\n260\t        ]\n261\t      }\n262\t    ],\n263\t    \"figures\": [],\n264\t    \"analysis\": \"Audit 是纯 hygiene 任务但在 median 档下至关重要——soundness score 3.5-4.5 的差异往往取决于 reviewer 是否信任作者的细节把控。AUROC 0.82 引用的歧义（CoNLL vs SciERC, N=8 vs N=16）如果 reviewer 自己算对不上会直接降 soundness 0.5 分。修复耗时 ~3h，全部是文本编辑，零实验成本。在 median tier 下这些修复是 necessary condition for 3.5 soundness——如果不修，可能跌到 3.0 (Findings boundary)。\\n\\n在 median 档下，audit 发现的矛盾是可修复的 housekeeping 问题，不影响核心结论但如果未修会被 reviewer 作为 soundness concern 扣分（A3 PARTIAL 中 reviewer 对 single-point ablation 的质疑部分源于数字不一致降低可信度）。最关键矛盾是 AUROC 0.82 的来源——paper_framing.md 中 Claim 1 说 'AUROC up to 0.82' 但实际最高是 CoNLL EM_AUROC=0.816 (exp_002) 或 CoNLL N=16 EM_AUROC=0.841 (exp_002_conll_n16)。Median tier soundness score 3.5-4.5 意味着这些矛盾被发现但不致命——修复后不影响结论但审稿时若未修会被扣 0.5 分。\"\n265\t  }\n266\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6243f3b-91fc-4875-8c31-fd34d0e76126","uuid":"05ae5d76-3f29-4e8b-9d9b-dcbb20d89e51","timestamp":"2026-05-16T11:45:10.319Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T113255/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ner_llama_conll\",\n    \"description\": \"LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003, N=8 inference. Cross-model validation for model-agnostic QE claims.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"greedy_f1\": 0.921,\n      \"oracle_f1\": 0.944,\n      \"oracle_headroom_pp\": 2.3,\n      \"SJ_rho_full\": 0.418,\n      \"FK_rho_full\": 0.405,\n      \"LP_rho_full\": 0.298,\n      \"EM_rho_full\": 0.421,\n      \"voting_conf_rho_full\": 0.413,\n      \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.694,\n      \"EM_AUROC\": 0.701,\n      \"LP_AUROC\": 0.752,\n      \"selection_SJ_f1\": 0.92,\n      \"selection_LP_f1\": 0.921,\n      \"selection_vs_greedy_pp\": -0.1,\n      \"structural_beats_surface\": true,\n      \"degeneracy_rate\": 0.55\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: LLaMA CoNLL-2003 QE Metrics (N=8, T=1.0)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"ρ_full\",\n          \"τ_full\",\n          \"AUROC\",\n          \"ECE\",\n          \"Sel_F1\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SJ\",\n            0.418,\n            0.372,\n            0.694,\n            0.112,\n            0.92\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FK\",\n            0.405,\n            0.361,\n            0.688,\n            0.108,\n            0.919\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EM\",\n            0.421,\n            0.377,\n            0.701,\n            0.105,\n            0.919\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Voting_conf\",\n            0.413,\n            0.368,\n            0.698,\n            0.092,\n            0.92\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Logprob\",\n            0.298,\n            0.238,\n            0.752,\n            0.131,\n            0.921\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Greedy\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.921\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Oracle\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.944\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model validation holds but provides incremental rather than decisive evidence. Reviewer likely notes: (1) both are 8B-class models — no evidence for smaller/larger scales; (2) CoNLL's high baseline makes selection analysis trivial (headroom <3pp). In median tier, this supports the QE contribution as 'solid engineering' (A1 PARTIAL) but doesn't push novelty score above 3-4 because the finding (structural signals generalize across architectures) is expected from UQ literature.\\n\\n在 median 档下，LLaMA CoNLL 复现 Qwen CoNLL 的核心模式（structural > surface，selection ≈ greedy），但不会显著超越。CoNLL 高 baseline F1 (>0.91) 导致高 degeneracy (~55%)，oracle headroom 仅 2.3pp，selection 无法显著超过 greedy。SJ_rho ~0.42 与 Qwen CoNLL (0.436) 一致，验证 cross-model 但 reviewer 会指出 '两个 8B 模型不足以证明 model-agnostic'——这正是 A6 PARTIAL 假设的体现。LP AUROC 偏高（0.75）因为 CoNLL 高精度实例的 LP 能有效区分 perfect vs near-perfect，但 rho 仍低于 structural signals。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"simple_verifier_baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"Logistic regression on 5 QE signals as supervised verifier. Tests whether oracle gap is closable with supervision. Training on SciERC NER+RE with F1 labels.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ner_verifier_selection_f1\": 0.655,\n      \"ner_greedy_f1\": 0.644,\n      \"ner_oracle_f1\": 0.776,\n      \"ner_gap_closure_pct\": 8.3,\n      \"ner_verifier_vs_greedy_pp\": 1.1,\n      \"re_verifier_selection_f1\": 0.412,\n      \"re_greedy_f1\": 0.404,\n      \"re_oracle_f1\": 0.585,\n      \"re_gap_closure_pct\": 4.4,\n      \"re_verifier_vs_greedy_pp\": 0.8,\n      \"cv_auroc_ner\": 0.772,\n      \"cv_auroc_re\": 0.718,\n      \"feature_importance_top\": \"EM > voting_conf > SJ > LP > FK\",\n      \"overfitting_risk\": \"moderate (n=529 NER, n=397 RE, 5-fold CV)\",\n      \"training_time_minutes\": 12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Supervised Verifier vs Unsupervised Signals (5-fold CV)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"NER Sel_F1\",\n          \"NER Δ_greedy\",\n          \"NER Gap%\",\n          \"RE Sel_F1\",\n          \"RE Δ_greedy\",\n          \"RE Gap%\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Greedy (T=0)\",\n            0.644,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.404,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Best unsupervised (LP)\",\n            0.65,\n            \"+0.6pp\",\n            \"4.5%\",\n            0.409,\n            \"+0.5pp\",\n            \"2.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LR verifier (5 signals)\",\n            0.655,\n            \"+1.1pp\",\n            \"8.3%\",\n            0.412,\n            \"+0.8pp\",\n            \"4.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Oracle\",\n            0.776,\n            \"+13.2pp\",\n            \"100%\",\n            0.585,\n            \"+18.1pp\",\n            \"100%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Feature Importance (Logistic Regression Coefficients, NER)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"Mean Coeff\",\n          \"Std across folds\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"EM\",\n            0.42,\n            0.08\n          ],\n          [\n            \"voting_conf\",\n            0.31,\n            0.06\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SJ\",\n            0.22,\n            0.09\n          ],\n          [\n            \"logprob\",\n            0.18,\n            0.11\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FK\",\n            0.07,\n            0.05\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Verifier closes 8.3% of NER gap — statistically significant (paired t-test p<0.05 across folds) but practically marginal. This is precisely the A5 WEAK outcome: enough to say 'supervision helps' but not enough to constitute a paper contribution. One reviewer will say 'you showed logistic regression on your own features slightly beats your own features used individually — this is expected and not interesting.' Counter-argument: the 92% gap that remains proves the signals are fundamentally limited, not just suboptimally combined. Paper frames as: 'preliminary supervised baseline confirms gap is partially closable, motivating dedicated learned verifiers as future work.' Findings-level contribution at best for this component.\\n\\n在 median 档下 (A5 FAILS/WEAK)，trained verifier 完成但 gap closure <15%。逻辑回归在 5 个高度相关的信号上（SJ-LP pearson=0.57）受限于 feature redundancy——exp-016 已经显示 ensemble 无优势。NER gap closure ~8% (1.1pp) 因为：(1) 监督信号确实比 unsupervised heuristic 好（能学到非线性组合），但 (2) 输入信号本身信息量有限（within-instance discriminative power 低），5-fold CV 在 n=529 上容易 overfit。RE 更弱 (4.4%) 因为 binary dominance (43% F1=0) 使得回归主要学到 'zero vs non-zero' 而非 quality gradient。Reviewer 评价：'path forward evidence suggestive not definitive'——8% closure 不足以作为独立贡献，但支持 'trained verifiers needed' 的 future work framing。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"claim_audit\",\n    \"description\": \"Systematic numerical consistency audit across all paper sections. Resolve contradictions between Discussion, Limitations, Abstract, and source experiment data.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"contradictions_found\": 4,\n      \"critical_contradictions\": 1,\n      \"minor_inconsistencies\": 3,\n      \"sections_affected\": [\n        \"Discussion\",\n        \"Limitations\",\n        \"Abstract\",\n        \"Introduction\"\n      ],\n      \"resolution_time_hours\": 3,\n      \"key_contradiction_1\": \"Discussion '+0.1pp over single-sample' vs Limitations '+0.4pp over greedy' — source truth is +0.6pp (logprob NER, exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap)\",\n      \"key_contradiction_2\": \"Abstract AUROC '0.82' refers to CoNLL EM (0.816) but body text reports SciERC EM (0.749) — need to clarify which dataset/metric the abstract claim uses\",\n      \"key_contradiction_3\": \"Introduction claims '5 confidence signals across 4 families' but method section describes 5 signals in 3 families (structural: SJ/FK/EM; voting: VC; probabilistic: LP)\",\n      \"key_contradiction_4\": \"Capability-degeneracy numbers: Discussion says 'CoNLL 58%' but exp_012_rerun_1024 shows tied_fraction=0.597 for constrained, referencing different definitions of degeneracy\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Claim Audit Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Location\",\n          \"Claimed Value\",\n          \"Source Truth\",\n          \"Resolution\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Abstract: 'AUROC up to 0.82'\",\n            \"0.82\",\n            \"CoNLL EM 0.816 (N=8) or 0.841 (N=16)\",\n            \"Use 0.82 rounded from 0.816, cite N=8 CoNLL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Discussion: '+0.1pp'\",\n            \"+0.1pp over single-sample\",\n            \"+0.6pp LP vs greedy (NER, p=0.39 n.s.)\",\n            \"Correct to '+0.6pp (n.s., p=0.39)'\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Limitations: '+0.4pp'\",\n            \"+0.4pp over greedy\",\n            \"Same metric different rounding\",\n            \"Unify to +0.6pp with CI\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Intro: '4 families'\",\n            \"4 signal families\",\n            \"3 families (structural/voting/probabilistic)\",\n            \"Correct to '3 families' or redefine EM as separate family\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Audit 是纯 hygiene 任务但在 median 档下至关重要——soundness score 3.5-4.5 的差异往往取决于 reviewer 是否信任作者的细节把控。AUROC 0.82 引用的歧义（CoNLL vs SciERC, N=8 vs N=16）如果 reviewer 自己算对不上会直接降 soundness 0.5 分。修复耗时 ~3h，全部是文本编辑，零实验成本。在 median tier 下这些修复是 necessary condition for 3.5 soundness——如果不修，可能跌到 3.0 (Findings boundary)。\\n\\n在 median 档下，audit 发现的矛盾是可修复的 housekeeping 问题，不影响核心结论但如果未修会被 reviewer 作为 soundness concern 扣分（A3 PARTIAL 中 reviewer 对 single-point ablation 的质疑部分源于数字不一致降低可信度）。最关键矛盾是 AUROC 0.82 的来源——paper_framing.md 中 Claim 1 说 'AUROC up to 0.82' 但实际最高是 CoNLL EM_AUROC=0.816 (exp_002) 或 CoNLL N=16 EM_AUROC=0.841 (exp_002_conll_n16)。Median tier soundness score 3.5-4.5 意味着这些矛盾被发现但不致命——修复后不影响结论但审稿时若未修会被扣 0.5 分。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":266,"startLine":1,"totalLines":266}}}
